specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:16:- For a session that completes without error the hooks fire in the order `beforeSession` → `beforeUserInput` → `afterUserInput` → `beforeModelResponse` → `afterModelResponse` → `afterSession` ([validated by: fires the lifecycle hooks in documented order for a session that completes without error](../../src/config.test.ts#L132)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:23:- `afterModelResponse` receives concatenated response text from every round ([validated by: joins the text of every round, not only the last](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L507)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:25:## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:27:- The `usage` handed to `afterModelResponse` is the sum of every provider call in the turn, so a turn that ran tool rounds reports the input, output and total tokens of all of them rather than of the last call alone ([validated by: reports 600 input, 60 output, 660 total for a two-tool-round turn whose calls report 100/10, 200/20 and 300/30](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L60)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:30:- The hook's third argument is `TurnUsageMetadata`, naming it as the sum for the whole turn ([validated by: names the usage passed to afterModelResponse as a turn total](../../src/orchestration/turnUsageType.test.ts#L6)).
